646</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17085383</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b6-ijms-10-02084"><label>6.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ling</surname><given-names>GN</given-names></name></person-group><source>Life at the cell and below-cell level. The hidden history of a fundamental revolution in biology</source><publisher-name>Pacific Press</publisher-name><publisher-loc>New York, NY, USA</publisher-loc><year>2001</year></citation></ref><ref id="b7-ijms-10-02084"><label>7.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pollack</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><source>Cells, gels and the engines of life: a new, unifying approach to cell function</source><publisher-name>Ebner and Sons</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Seattle, WA, USA</publisher-loc><year>2001</year></citation></ref><ref id="b8-ijms-10-02084"><label>8.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bianconi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A statistical mechanics approach for scale-free networks and finite-scale networks</article-title><source>Chaos</source><year>2007</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>026114</fpage><lpage>026116</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17614701</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b9-ijms-10-02084"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bianconi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The entropy of network ensembles</article-title><source>Phys. Rev. E</source><year>2009</year><volume>79</volume><fpage>036114</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b10-ijms-10-02084"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="book" id="N0x1d110a0N0x21e9630"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kauffman</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><source>The origins of order: self organization and selection in evolution</source><publisher-name>Oxford University Press</publisher-name><publisher-loc>New York, USA</publisher-loc><year>1993</year></citation><citation citation-type="journal" id="N0x1d110a0N0x21e9750">ibidem <source>J. Theor. Bio</source><year>1969</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>437</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5803332</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="journal" id="N0x1d110a0N0x21e97b0"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kadanoff</surname><given-names>LP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Hip Bone is connected to II Phys</article-title><source>Today</source><year>2009</year><volume>62</volume><fpage>8</fpage><lpage>9</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b11-ijms-10-02084"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rupley</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Siemankowski</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Careri</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bruni</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Two-dimensional protonic percolation on lightly hydrated purple membrane</article-title><source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA</source><year>1988</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>9022</fpage><lpage>9025</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16593999</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12-ijms-10-02084"><label>12.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bianconi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Barabasi</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bose-Einstein condensation in complex networks</article-title><source>Phys. Rev. Lett</source><year>2001</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>5632</fpage><lpage>5635</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11415319</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13-ijms-10-02084"><label>13.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bianconi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Emergence of weight-topology correlations in complex networks</article-title><source>Europhys. Lett</source><year>2005</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>1029</fpage><lpage>1035</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b14-ijms-10-02084"><label>14.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ferretti</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bianconi</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dynamics of condensation in growing complex networks</article-title><source>Phys. Rev. E</source><year>2008</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>056102</fpage><lpage>056107</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b15-ijms-10-02084"><label>15.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Engel</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Calhoun</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Read</surname><given-names>EL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahn</surname><given-names>TK</given-names></name><name><surname>Mancal</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheng</surname><given-names>YC</given-names></name><name><surname>Blankenship</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Fleming</surname><given-names>GR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evidence for wavelike energy transfer through quantum coherence in photosynthetic systems</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2007</year><volume>446</volume><fpage>782</fpage><lpage>786</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17429397</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16-ijms-10-02084"><label>16.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hagan</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Hameroff</surname><given-names>SR</given-names></name><name><surname>Tuszyn</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Quantum computation in brain microtubules: Decoherence and biological feasibility</article-title><source>Phys. Rev. E</source><year>2002</year><volume>65</volume><fpage>061901</fpage><lpage>0619012</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b17-ijms-10-02084"><label>17.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Coleman</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Frontier at your fingertips</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>2007</year><volume>446</volume><fpage>379</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17377567</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18-ijms-10-02084"><label>18.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barrow</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Davies</surname><given-names>PCW</given-names></name><name><surname>Davies Harper</surname><given-names>CL</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name></person-group><source>Science and ultimate reality quantum theory, cosmology, and complexity</source><publisher-name>Cambridge University Press</publisher-name><publisher-loc>Cambridge, UK</publisher-loc><year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="b19-ijms-10-02084"><label>19.</label><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Davies</surname><given-names>PCW</given-names></name></person-group><source>Quantum fluctuations and life</source> Preprint arXiv:quant-ph/0403017, <year>2004</year></citation></ref><ref id="b20-ijms-10-02084"><label>20.</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Newman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Barab&#x000e1;si</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Watt</surname><given-names>